# Secure storage & key derivation

## The non-negotiable invariant

**Every fresh install MUST derive a unique, unpredictable seed.** A fixed,
deterministic, or low-entropy seed in a shipped build lets anyone reconstruct a
user's keys and drain their funds. There is no recovery from this — treat any
path that could feed a known seed into a production build as a P0 vulnerability.

## How the guarantee is currently held (verified 2026-06)

1. **CSPRNG is real, and loaded first.** Fresh seeds come from
   `crypto.getRandomValues(entropy)` over 16 bytes →
   `bip39.entropyToMnemonic` (`shared/lib/nostr/secureStorage.ts` `generateMnemonic`).
   `crypto.getRandomValues` is backed by `react-native-get-random-values`, imported
   as the **first** line of both `shim.js` and `index.js` (before any crypto
   consumer), with `react-native-quick-crypto` installed for `crypto.subtle`.
   If the polyfill were ever missing, `getRandomValues` throws → seed generation
   throws → `ensureMnemonicExists` returns `null` (no seed) — it **fails loud, never
   weak**. Do not "fall back" to `Math.random`, a constant, or any non-CSPRNG.

2. **The only non-random seed path is the debug override, and it is double-gated.**
   `getDebugMnemonicOverride()` returns `null` unless `__DEV__` (runtime, dead-stripped
   in release), AND `app.config.js` only writes `extra.debugMnemonic` when
   `buildProfile === 'development'` (stricter than `isDevelopment`, which also
   includes `preview`). The value comes from the **non-`EXPO_PUBLIC_`** `DEBUG_MNEMONIC`
   var so Expo never inlines it into a bundle. Pinned by
   `__tests__/appConfigDebugMnemonic.test.ts` (default/production/preview all reject it).

## Rules

- **Never** read a seed/mnemonic/nsec from an `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` env var — those are
  inlined verbatim into every bundle. Use `extra` via `app.config.js` with a
  `buildProfile` gate, and `__DEV__` at the read site.
- **Never** introduce a constant/test/"abandon abandon…" mnemonic into code that
  any non-`development` profile can reach. Debug seeds belong behind both gates above.
- Secrets (mnemonic, nsec, 64-hex private keys) are stored only in SecureStore
  (`storeMnemonic`, `storeImportedNsec`) — never AsyncStorage, never logs. See the
  redaction layer in `shared/lib/loggerCore.ts`.
- A corrupt/invalid stored mnemonic is surfaced (`null` + loud log), **never**
  silently overwritten — the user is the sole holder of the seed.

## When you add a new key/seed path

Add a test that proves no fixed value can reach `preview`/`production`, and extend
this doc. A new way to inject a known seed is the kind of regression
`skill:critical-failures` exists to catch.
